  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday) \nIssued at 131 AM MDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nBy Tuesday and Wednesday, the upper high gets kicked much farther \neast while an upper level low/trough moves from the Pac NW into\nthe Great Basin. The door opens for a monsoon burst pattern to \nsurge north into NM with 90th %tile PWATs for mid September at \nKABQ (>1.2\"). Several perturbations are shown by extended models \nmoving north from MX with numerous to widespread showers and \nstorms for our region. The upper level low/trough over the Great \nBasin moves east across the central Rockies on Thursday and Friday\nand helps to provide greater forcing/ascent for more showers and \nstorms over the southern Rockies. The 4-day QPF is impressive with\njust about the entire region progged to receive >1.25\". Locally \nhigher amounts from the NBM 90th %tile and WPC are >3\". The flood \nrisk will increase with each passing day of heavy rain. However, \nit is still extremely dry in many areas so impacts may be confined\nto areas with training storms, burn scars, urban areas, and low-\nlying areas. Forecast confidence is increasing slightly but is \nstill only moderate given the consistently underwhelming \nperformance of this monsoon season. Confidence is higher that \ntemps will trend closer to normal for mid September with greater \ncloud cover and higher humidity.",
